-- title:
--   Fundamental character of level two for non-unit Tₚ, p odd
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero level with $p \nmid M$, and let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p \in S$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field, and with $p$ lying in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi_0$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {p})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$ outside $S \setminus \{p\}$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$ outside $S \setminus \{p\}$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$, and assume $\chi_0(T_p)$ is not a unit (the operator $T_p$ being available since $p \nmid M$ and $p \notin S \setminus \{p\}$); assume also $p \neq 2$. The assertion is that there is a ring $\mathcal{O}''$ of the same type (a characteristic-zero adically complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field) which is an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra, finite as an $\mathcal{O}'$-module, with local and injective structure map, and a rank-two adic Galois representation $\rho_0$ over $\mathcal{O}''$ — a free finite $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}(V)$ such that for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ has $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n V$ for all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise — with the following two properties. First, for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \notin S$ (and $\ell \notin S \setminus \{p\}$), every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a non-unit, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition group of $A$ and acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho_0.\rho\,\sigma$ is $X^2 - \chi_0(T_\ell)X + \ell$, the coefficients being taken in $\mathcal{O}''$ through the structure map. Second, for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $p$ is a non-unit and every $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\pi^{p^2-1} = p$, there are a ring homomorphism $\psi$ from the residue field of $\mathcal{O}''$ to the residue field of $P$ and a nonzero vector $v$ in the base change along $\psi$ of the residual representation $\rho_0$.`residual` (the residue field of $\mathcal{O}''$ tensored with $V$) such that either $\rho(\sigma)v = \mathrm{tameCharacter}_P(\pi)(\sigma)\, v$ for all $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$, or $\rho(\sigma)v = \mathrm{tameCharacter}_P(\pi)(\sigma)^{p}\, v$ for all such $\sigma$, where the tame character sends $\sigma$ to the residue class of $\sigma\pi/\pi$ when that lies in $P$ and to $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the modular input for the supersingular side of the local analysis at $p$: the Galois representation attached to a Hecke eigensystem with non-unit $T_p$ is, on inertia above $p$, described by a fundamental character of level two, realised here through the tame character at a uniformiser $\pi$ with $\pi^{p^2-1}=p$ and its $p$-th power. It is used in [`CuspForm.point_residual_stable_eq_bot_or_top_of_not_isUnit_heckeT_of_ne_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.point_residual_stable_eq_bot_or_top_of_not_isUnit_heckeT_of_ne_two) and in [`GaloisRep.exists_inertia_eigenvector_tameCharacter_pow_of_theta_heckeT_eq_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_two`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_inertia_eigenvector_tameCharacter_pow_of_theta_heckeT_eq_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_eq_two).
